# Pre-push & Lovable / Supabase sync

Before you **finish a task**, **suggest pushing**, or **confirm a branch is ready to merge**, treat [docs/ops/deployment-sync-guide.md](docs/ops/deployment-sync-guide.md) as the canonical checklist. Summarize or run the relevant steps; do not skip them for "small" changes if they touch migrations, edge functions, Supabase types, or production behavior.

## Minimum commands (when code changed)

Run and address failures before push:

- `npm run test`
- `npm run build`
- `npm run lint` on touched files (whole-repo lint has known noise)
- `npm run check:edge` when Deno is available (edge TS changes)

## Always remember

| What | Effect on sync |
|------|----------------|
| `supabase/migrations/` | Applied to **production DB** when GitHub syncs |
| `supabase/functions/` + `config.toml` | Edge functions deploy to **production** |
| `src/` frontend | **Not** live until **Publish → Update** in Lovable |

- New `[functions.*]` block in `supabase/config.toml` for every new edge function (same PR).
- New columns queried before `types.ts` regenerates: use `as unknown as YourRow[]` (see deployment guide).
- Destructive migrations: order-of-operations per the guide (code ↔ schema).

If the user asks only to "push" or "ship," still verify the checklist or state what was skipped and why.
